WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
Satoshi and Go have arrived in Galar
to accomplish a particular task.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:14.080
At Shoot City Station, they boarded
a Ghost Train carrying Ghost-type Pokémon.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.960
Together with a mysterious boy
wearing a mask,

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:21.580
Satoshi and Go managed to calm down
a rampaging Mikaruge.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:26.630
Then, they finally arrived
in Lateral Town, in Galar.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.260
Now, what could
this particular task be?

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.350
I can’t wait!

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.470
Let’s try our best, Gänger!

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.890
You’re both really excited, huh?

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.440
Yeah! I mean...

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.940
So that’s Kyodaimax Gänger...

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.610
It’s really cool! Right?

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.580
Director Sakuragi!
How can I make my Gänger Kyodaimax?

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.370
Hmm... Good question...

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:03.540
Why don’t you try visiting Onion,
the Gym Leader of Lateral Town’s Ghost Gym?

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.420
Onion at the Ghost Gym!

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.590
We’re gonna have him
teach us Kyodaimax!

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:16.180
Still, I never knew Lateral Town
had two Gyms in it.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:21.850
Ms. Saito’s Gym is one of them, and then
there’s the one just around the corner... Huh?

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.440
<i>That’s</i> the Ghost Gym?!

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:41.790
This... is the right place...

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.750
But I don’t see a door anywhere...

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:48.090
Let’s just try calling him!

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:53.590
Excuse me!
Mr. Onion, are you there?!

00:01:53.590 --> 00:02:00.020
We wanna ask you something
about Gänger!

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:03.230
Maybe he’s not here?

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:13.240
Don’t yell my name out...
so loudly...

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:14.610
Huh?

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.080
That boy from yesterday...

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:21.580
Oh, so you’re Onion!

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:22.580
Hey—

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:24.580
Wha...?

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.980
Oh, you really surprised us!

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:08.600
You didn’t answer at all, Onion!

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:11.610
And we had no idea
how to open the door.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:14.570
Then, next to this stain
that looked like a face, you...

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:15.860
Satoshi!

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:16.360
Hmm?

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.030
It looks like Onion’s
trying to say something.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:21.490
Oh, sorry! What is it?

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:24.490
What you said...

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:25.370
Huh?

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.870
Wanting to ask me about Gänger...

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:30.880
Right! You see...

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.710
We want to Kyodaimax!

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:37.550
You... want to, as well?

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.640
I see...

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.890
Where are you going?

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:49.560
It’s too cramped here, so...

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.730
The stadium.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:03.780
Saito!

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.240
Satoshi.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.040
Here for another battle?

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:13.170
No, today I’m here for
Kyodaimax training with Gänger.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:15.550
We’re having Onion help us!

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:17.380
Is that so?

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:23.510
Give it all you’ve got.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:24.890
Yeah!

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:34.560
Okay, give it a try...

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:35.820
Okay!

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:36.820
Let’s go, Gänger!

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.840
Let’s get huge! Kyodaimax!

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:13.230
Huh? But that’s...

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:21.360
No, that’s not Kyodaimax Gänger...

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:24.990
Go on! Go for it!

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.950
Almost there, Gänger!

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:33.870
It looks like it’s trying to force
a Kyodaimax-ish image.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:37.000
Satoshi.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.840
That was a shock.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:43.170
That Gänger can only Daimax.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.930
No matter how far you push it,
it can’t Kyodaimax.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:56.900
But if it drinks Dai Soup,
it can Kyodaimax.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:00.020
I think I’ve heard of that!

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:01.780
Here it is!

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:07.160
If a Pokémon drinks Dai Soup
made from Dai Mushrooms, it can Kyodaimax!

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:07.910
Hear that?

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:12.500
Then let’s have you drink
that Dai Soup and Kyodaimax, Gänger!

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:17.040
So... Where can we find
Dai Mushrooms, Onion?

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:19.170
In the woods...

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:22.050
Got it! Come with us!

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:25.420
B-But...
They won’t be easy to get...

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:26.090
Huh?

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:26.930
Why?

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:33.270
Those woods are home to tons
of Ghost-type Pokémon...

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:36.480
They can all be very quirky...

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:38.560
Quirky...

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.650
They’ll try to stop you.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:44.780
It’ll be fine!
Nothing’s gonna stop me from getting ‘em!

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.200
A g-graveyard...?

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.290
Are there Dai Mushrooms here?

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.080
Yeah.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:59.080
There are Galar Particles
gathered here.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.460
Right in the back.

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:02.840
Those are Dai Mushrooms.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:11.390
Hey, those quirky Pokémon
you mentioned earlier...

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:13.850
The stones in the graveyard...

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:18.600
There’s Galarian Sunnygo
mixed in with them.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.600
Huh?

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:26.360
Sunnygo! Galarian Form!
Coral Pokémon! Ghost type!

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:29.860
Sudden climate change wiped out
this ancient kind of Sunnygo!

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:33.120
If you mistake it for a stone and kick it,
it will curse you!

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:34.990
So...

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:39.500
You must...
never kick them...

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:45.460
But we don’t even know
which ones are Galarian Sunnygo...

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:46.880
How can we...?

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.090
I just had a great idea!

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:53.100
We can float over
to the Dai Mushrooms!

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:56.390
Then we can get ‘em
without kicking any Galarian Sunnygo, right?

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:59.770
Y-Yeah, that looks like it...
might work...

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:01.520
I’m counting on you, Gänger!

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:05.690
Just be careful, Satoshi!

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:07.940
If you happen to fall off...

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:11.700
I’m fine, I’m fine!

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.290
Just... a little further...

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:27.760
All right!

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.800
All done!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.230
That’s a Galarian Sunnygo.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.400
Sorry about that.

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:50.610
Th-This isn’t good!
I-I-It’s gonna curse you!

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:04.710
Sunnygo: Galarian Form’s data
will be added to the Index!

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:07.710
I just barely saved it...

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:10.130
Glad you got my back, Go!

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:12.420
With your help,
I got the Dai Mushrooms!

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:15.760
Now we can make
our Dai Soup...

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.220
Not yet.

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:22.020
Those won’t be enough
to make Dai Soup.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:27.570
Mushrooms! Hey, mushrooms!

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:32.610
You found some?!

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:35.990
I don’t see any Ghost Pokémon...

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:37.780
Okay! Let’s go, Gänger!

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.540
Oh, that’s...

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.330
I got ‘em, no sweat!

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:48.750
What’s that...?!

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:54.340
Ohrot! Elder Tree Pokémon!
Ghost/Grass type!

00:10:54.340 --> 00:11:01.600
It extends thin roots from the tips of its feet and
ties them into the trees of the forest to control them!

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:05.770
No Pokémon in these woods
hates humans more than Ohrot.

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:06.400
What?!

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:18.870
Satoshi, hurry this way!

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:20.120
It’s after us, too?!

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:23.370
Run for it, you guys!
We’ve gotta get away!

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:35.260
We made it out, somehow...

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:37.470
Now we have two clusters
of Dai Mushrooms.

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:39.930
So, will this be enough?

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:42.970
No...
You’ll need a little more.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.020
Dai Mushrooms!

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:53.610
...with something on them?

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:00.910
It’s using the mushrooms
as a pillow!

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:05.410
Yeah.
This one likes Dai Mushrooms.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:10.290
Draunch! Caretaker Pokémon!
Dragon/Ghost type!

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:12.340
It can fly at 200 kilometers per hour!

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:15.590
It battles alongside Drameshiya
and dotes on them!

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:19.010
Drameshiya...
Is that this guy?

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:39.990
It’s like it’s still half-asleep!

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:42.950
That’s really cute.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.000
Oh, it woke up.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:03.390
Without a Drameshiya on its head, it gets so uneasy
that it may try to use another Pokémon as a substitute!

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:10.730
Hey, stop that, Sarunori!

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:22.570
What now?

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:23.950
What indeed...

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:36.420
Sarunori!
It’s trying to shake you off!

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:38.010
Hold on tight!

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:39.630
We’ve gotta do something...

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.930
You have to give that one back to it.

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:42.720
Got it.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:49.180
Draunch!
Your Drameshiya is over here!

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:58.030
Watch out! Satoshi!

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:02.320
Pocket Monsters!

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:17.710
Draunch!
Your Drameshiya is over here!

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:24.720
Watch out! Satoshi!

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:44.200
Thanks, Gänger!

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:49.870
You okay, Sarunori?

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:51.410
Now, don’t go falling off again.

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:04.170
Sorry for disturbing your nap.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:09.350
That tickles!

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:12.020
Hey, Draunch...

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:15.810
That boy wants to have
your mushrooms.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:26.660
Are you sure?

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:29.700
It says yes.

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:32.700
Really? Thanks!

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:35.830
Now we can make the Dai Soup.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:37.830
We did it, Gänger!

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.170
Yay!

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.150
Now it just needs
to stew overnight.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:08.070
Thank you, Onion.

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:10.070
I didn’t do anything.

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:11.870
This was all you.

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:16.540
Yes, you really
worked hard today.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:22.340
Are you sure you didn’t hurt yourself
when you stopped that Draunch earlier?

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:27.090
That’s a relief, then.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:31.350
Hey, Onion...
Can you speak with Pokémon?

00:16:33.850 --> 00:16:39.060
That’s right! On the Ghost Train,
you knew what Mikaruge was saying.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:41.230
Same with the Draunch
and Drameshiya.

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:41.860
Yeah!

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:44.860
You don’t...

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:47.610
...think I’m weird?

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:48.740
No way!

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:50.360
If anything, I’m jealous!

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:51.200
Huh?

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:56.120
I mean, Satoshi, you can work out
what Pokémon are trying to say too, right?

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:57.250
Yeah.

00:16:57.250 --> 00:17:01.750
Sometimes when we’re battling together,
our hearts go “clang!” and connect,

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:05.630
and “bang!”, it’s like we start
thinking the same things.

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:09.380
Oh, of course.
Clanging and banging, right...

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:11.800
You’re weird.

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:17.310
Anyway, I never would’ve
made it this far without you!

00:17:17.310 --> 00:17:19.890
So now you can leave
watching the pot to me!

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:21.900
It’ll be safe and sound with me!

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:32.030
That’s more like
<i>sleeping</i> soundly...

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:35.160
Satoshi is rather fun.

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:40.120
Yeah. He’s a lot of fun,
and a really nice guy!

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:45.750
You can go to sleep.
I’ll watch the soup.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.130
Okay, got it.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:10.820
You mustn’t open that.

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:13.160
Don’t worry.

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:18.290
You and Satoshi worked really hard
collecting those Dai Mushrooms.

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:21.040
I know they’ll make for
a great Dai Soup.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:29.710
I think I finally get why you kept saying
you wanted to get stronger.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:34.840
You want to stay
by Satoshi’s side, right?

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:41.430
You’ve been through lonely times,
but now everything is looking up.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:51.360
Now that you’ve met someone who really
cares for you, and works together with you.

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:05.710
Th-That’s enough.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:08.460
I know you’re happy.

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:11.340
Hey, I get it...

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:20.510
Dai Soup!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.600
Go ahead.

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.910
Now go and give it a try.

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.040
Let’s go, Gänger!

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:56.010
This is unusual.

00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:59.720
I don’t see you helping
someone very often.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:12.320
Let’s get huge! Kyodaimax!

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:27.210
That’s Kyodaimax Gänger!

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:30.710
We did it!

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:33.040
It worked perfectly, Satoshi!

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:40.260
You really... managed it...

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:47.060
Wait, wait, wait!

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:48.730
Wait, wait! Wait!

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:50.940
Please refrain from running
to catch the train.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:57.110
Onion?

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:01.740
You came to see us off!

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:07.750
Hey! Uh...

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:12.290
I had so much more I wanted
to talk about, but um, how should I put it...?

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:15.090
Thanks for everything, Onion!

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:19.550
See you again!

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:20.760
See ya!

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:27.020
Yeah. Until next time.

00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:30.890
The shy Onion.

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:34.900
With his help,
Gänger managed to Kyodaimax.

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:39.280
We’ve seen the beginning of huge memories,
and a huge friendship.

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:09.700
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:13.710
Whenever there is a meeting,
a parting is sure to follow.

00:23:14.410 --> 00:23:16.500
Everything that exists
will disappear in the course of time.

00:23:17.750 --> 00:23:20.380
And that is what makes
all of the bonds that connect us...

00:23:20.380 --> 00:23:23.260
...each so precious,
and each so painful.

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:24.720
Do you remember...

00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:28.970
...that place,
where we first met?

00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:31.600
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.600 --> 00:23:34.270
Your Name is Françoise
